WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
Speaker 1: Let's see if we can squeeze&nbsp;
in another call. What about Cameron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.800
from Seattle, Washington? Cameron. Go.
Speaker 3: Hello? David, can you hear me?&nbsp;

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.080
Speaker 1: Yes, I can.
Speaker 3: Nice. It was very nice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.920
to talk to you on this Friday morning.
Speaker 1: Likewise. Did you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.200
have a question today?
Speaker 3: Yes. I know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.840
you've expressed your interest in term limits&nbsp;
for Congressman, but what do you think about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.360
term limits for Supreme Court justices?
Speaker 1: I am in favor of it as well.&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:38.720
Speaker 3: Yes. What? What? How&nbsp;
many years would be a good term?&nbsp;

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:45.840
Speaker 1: So one proposal I read suggests that&nbsp;
12 is a good number because with nine Supreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:52.400
Court justices, you can create a cycle that makes&nbsp;
sense overlapping it with four year presidential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.080
terms. I don't know that 12 is actually the&nbsp;
number, but it could be. It was either 12 or 15.&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.440
Speaker 3: Yeah. That makes sense.
Speaker 1: That sounds reasonable.&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:08.240
Speaker 3: I had. Yeah. Sorry for taking my call.
Speaker 1: Appreciate it. Thank you very much.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.040
And on that note, that does it for calls&nbsp;
today. I am never able to speak to everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.840
and I apologize for that. But I will take&nbsp;
calls again and hope to hear from more of you.

